// spec: CLS-014
//
// A superclass must BE a class.
//
// ⚠️ This is the case that makes hoisting a class harder than hoisting a
// function.  A class declaration EVALUATES its superclass, so hoisting the
// declaration would hoist the evaluation -- and then 'X' would not yet hold 1,
// and this diagnostic would be unreachable for any name declared in the same
// file.  The name is bound at hoist time and the superclass is resolved where
// the declaration STANDS, which is what keeps this reachable.

var X := 1;

class C (X);
begin
end
